    "statement": "Implement `normalize_protection(ranges, edits, max_row, max_col)`.\n\nEach element of `ranges` is an inclusive rectangle `(r1, c1, r2, c2)` of protected cells within a fixed worksheet of `max_row` by `max_col` cells. Rectangles may overlap or touch and collectively denote their union.\n\nApply every edit in `edits`, in order. An edit is `(axis, index, delta)`, where `axis` is `\"row\"` or `\"column\"` and `delta != 0`. Coordinates on the other axis are unchanged.\n\nFor `delta > 0`, insert `delta` unprotected lines immediately before `index`. Existing cells before `index` stay fixed, cells at or after `index` move by `delta`, and cells moved beyond the fixed worksheet boundary are discarded.\n\nFor `delta < 0`, let `d = -delta`. Delete lines `index` through `index+d-1`. Cells in them disappear, later cells move by `-d`, and the final `d` lines become unprotected. Thus worksheet dimensions never change.\n\nEvery edit is valid when it is applied: `1 <= index <=` the relevant dimension, and a deletion interval lies entirely within that dimension. Inserted lines can be affected by later edits but remain unprotected unless protected content is subsequently moved onto their coordinates. Protection bel",
